\pard\b\fs42 Baguette Production Planning and Daily Capacity\b0\fs22\par\par \pard\sb200\sa140\keepn\b\fs28 H3 ingredient correction\b0\fs22\par \pard\sa120 EDC is not butter and must not be treated or priced as margarine. Its identity, specification, permitted application, dose and purchase price remain unresolved. Keep EDC as a separate historical ingredient and hold affected formulas until it is identified. The earlier owner-workbook butter-to-margarine instruction remains separate; true dairy butter in independent recipes retains its specification. Milk tantalizer and improver remain omitted from revised recipes.\par \pard\sa120 T01 cake doughnuts and H05 Danisa biscuits are held. Ninety-two historical formula variants retain EDC separately and unpriced. The lean baguette programme BAG-H2-01 contains no EDC and its formula and timing assumptions are unchanged. H3 supersedes the EDC interpretation in H1 and H2; original editions are retained only as historical records.\par \pard\sa120 H2 planning module \u8226? 8 October 2026 \u8226? Nkambe, Cameroon \u8226? All clock times are local bakery planning times.\par \pard\sb200\sa140\keepn\b\fs28 Decision and source identification\b0\fs22\par \pard\sa120 The requested document was located: Staggered_Baguette_Production_Schedule.pdf, source S038, in the owner's Downloads folder. It has two pages and was modified on 11 September 2026. Its filename describes scheduling; its internal heading is \u8220?Commercial Baguette Production Guide\u8221?. This is the closest direct match, supported by the five-batch programmes in S026 and S027. Current file hashes match the H1 source inventory.\par \pard\sa120 S038 describes two 80-piece batches. S026/S027 extend related reasoning to five batches of allegedly 101 pieces each, implying 505 pieces in a production campaign. That is a source claim, not a verified daily output. No sales orders, successful timed campaign, installed rack count or signed production record were supplied.\par \pard\sa120 H2 retains the useful idea of staggered mixing and converts it into whole-load programmes. It does not adopt the source's contradictory clocks, unverified equipment claims or immediate closed-box packing. The new recipe BAG-H2-01 is a separate direct-dough commercial trial; existing M1-B12, M1-B13 and S-B01 remain separate formulas.\par \trowd\trgaph70\trhdr\cellx3333\cellx6667\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 \b Source\b0 \cell \pard\intbl\fs18 \b Relevant evidence\b0 \cell \pard\intbl\fs18 \b Decision\b0 \cell \row \trowd\trgaph70\cellx3333\cellx6667\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 S038\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 PDF p1 formulation/cadence; p2 two-rack timeline and controls\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Primary requested scheduling document; correct arithmetic and sequencing\cell \row \trowd\trgaph70\cellx3333\cellx6667\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 S030\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 PDF pp1\u8211?2; 80-piece formula and industrial workflow\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Formula/process companion; contains the same yield discrepancy\cell \row \trowd\trgaph70\cellx3333\cellx6667\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 S027\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 PDF pp1\u8211?2; five-batch checklist, 18 kg flour and 101 pieces/batch\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Retain implied 505-piece target as historical; rack and timing claims rejected\cell \row \trowd\trgaph70\cellx3333\cellx6667\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 S026\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Lines 9\u8211?29 schedule; 33\u8211?70 staff/logistics; subsequent water/ice discussion\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Useful duty and distribution concepts; reject hot airtight packing and unqualified par-bake route\cell \row \trowd\trgaph70\cellx3333\cellx6667\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 S001\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 PDF p1 audit and section 4 baguette system\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Earlier corrections are supporting analysis, not a production test\cell \row \trowd\trgaph70\cellx3333\cellx6667\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 S131 / S137\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Equipment sections and two-site business plans\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Broad operating context; not the requested baguette-specific programme\cell \row \pard\fs22\par \trowd\trgaph70\trhdr\cellx3333\cellx6667\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 \b ID\b0 \cell \pard\intbl\fs18 \b Document\b0 \cell \pard\intbl\fs18 \b Full path\b0 \cell \row \trowd\trgaph70\cellx3333\cellx6667\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 S038\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Staggered_Baguette_Production_Schedule.pdf\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 C:\\Users\\J COMPUTER\\Downloads\\Staggered_Baguette_Production_Schedule.pdf\cell \row \trowd\trgaph70\cellx3333\cellx6667\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 S030\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Commercial_Baguette_Production_Guide.pdf\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 C:\\Users\\J COMPUTER\\Downloads\\Commercial_Baguette_Production_Guide.pdf\cell \row \trowd\trgaph70\cellx3333\cellx6667\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 S027\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Bakery_Empire_Master_Operations_Manual.pdf\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 C:\\Users\\J COMPUTER\\Downloads\\Bakery_Empire_Master_Operations_Manual.pdf\cell \row \trowd\trgaph70\cellx3333\cellx6667\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 S026\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Bakery_Empire_Master_Operations_Manual.md\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 C:\\Users\\J COMPUTER\\Downloads\\Bakery_Empire_Master_Operations_Manual.md\cell \row \trowd\trgaph70\cellx3333\cellx6667\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 S001\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 bakery_strategy_and_recipe_manual_updated.pdf\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 C:\\Users\\J COMPUTER\\Documents\\Codex\\2026-09-12\\x20-go\\docs\\bakery\\bakery_strategy_and_recipe_manual_updated.pdf\cell \row \trowd\trgaph70\cellx3333\cellx6667\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 S131\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Nkambe_Bakery_Business_and_Production_Plan.pdf\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 C:\\Users\\J COMPUTER\\WPS Cloud Files\\.3728209773449\\cachedata\\2B0BE17ABD444588A82615757DB640F5\\Nkambe_Bakery_Business_and_Production_Plan.pdf\cell \row \trowd\trgaph70\cellx3333\cellx6667\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 S137\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Nkambe_Bakery_Business_and_Production_Plan.pdf\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 C:\\Users\\J COMPUTER\\WPS Cloud Files\\.3728209773449\\cachedata\\D084D8E5B0104800B3A610A601B8DF7B\\Nkambe_Bakery_Business_and_Production_Plan.pdf\cell \row \pard\fs22\par \pard\sb200\sa140\keepn\b\fs28 Source audit and corrected calculations\b0\fs22\par \trowd\trgaph70\trhdr\cellx3333\cellx6667\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 \b Topic\b0 \cell \pard\intbl\fs18 \b Original claim / input\b0 \cell \pard\intbl\fs18 \b H2 correction\b0 \cell \row \trowd\trgaph70\cellx3333\cellx6667\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 Ingredient total\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 S038 lists flour 14.20 kg, water 9.37 kg, salt 284 g, yeast 71 g.\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Sum = 23.925 kg. At exactly 66% water, water would be 9.372 kg and total 23.927 kg. Neither is 24 kg.\cell \row \trowd\trgaph70\cellx3333\cellx6667\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 Whole pieces\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 S038 says the batch yields exactly 80 \u215? 300 g.\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 23,925 / 300 = 79 pieces and 225 g left before handling loss. With 1% handling loss: 23,685.75 g \u8594? 78 pieces and 285.75 g left.\cell \row \trowd\trgaph70\cellx3333\cellx6667\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 Cooled weight\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 300 g raw is described as 250 g at 15% bake loss.\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 300 \u215? 0.85 = 255 g. A mathematical 250 g target at 15% loss requires 294.118 g raw, before portion and process variation.\cell \row \trowd\trgaph70\cellx3333\cellx6667\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 18 kg flour variant\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 S027 uses 18 kg flour, 8.28 kg water, 3.6 kg ice, 360 g salt, 90 g yeast.\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Total 30.330 kg, hydration 66% including ice. Before handling loss: 101 pieces + 30 g. At 1% loss: 100 pieces + 26.7 g.\cell \row \trowd\trgaph70\cellx3333\cellx6667\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 Five-batch output\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Five batches are claimed to yield 505 baguettes.\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 With 1% handling loss and 300 g portions, five 18 kg-flour batches give 500 pieces before rejects. At 80/load, 7 pooled loads are needed; if every batch is kept separate, 10 loads (80+20 per batch). Proofing must be redesigned for either route.\cell \row \trowd\trgaph70\cellx3333\cellx6667\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 Rack geometry\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 101 pieces are treated like one 16-tray load.\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 16 \u215? 5 = 80. 101 requires at least 21 trays at 5/tray. It cannot fit the assumed one-load geometry.\cell \row \trowd\trgaph70\cellx3333\cellx6667\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 Proof window\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 S038 p2 starts batch 1 proof at elapsed 01:30, promises 60 min, but loads at 02:15.\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 That window is 45 min. Batch 2 proof 02:15\u8211?03:15 is 60 min. H2 uses a common explicit 60-minute planning slot, subject to dough endpoint.\cell \row \trowd\trgaph70\cellx3333\cellx6667\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 Remaining times\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 At 00:45, S038 says batch 1 has 27 min left in bulk; its bulk actually ends 01:03.\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 18 min remain. Several remaining-time and overlap annotations disagree with their own start/end times.\cell \row \trowd\trgaph70\cellx3333\cellx6667\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 Cadence\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 S038 calls the oven cycle 25 min, prescribes 45-minute mixing starts, then shows first/second oven starts 60 min apart.\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 These are three different intervals. H2 reserves 40 minutes for scoring/loading, baking, unloading and recovery; 45-minute starts leave 5 minutes of nominal slack.\cell \row \trowd\trgaph70\cellx3333\cellx6667\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 Recovery\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 S038 alternates 3-minute recovery and a mandatory 23-minute thermal recovery statement.\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Neither is a measured requirement. Time actual recovery; H2 provisionally reserves 5 min after unloading. If 23 min is actually required, the H2 45-min cadence fails.\cell \row \trowd\trgaph70\cellx3333\cellx6667\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 Mix rest\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 A 10-minute rest with yeast already included is labelled autolyse.\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 H2 calls it a hydrated-dough rest. A flour/water-only autolyse is a different method and must not be inserted as extra time without revising the schedule.\cell \row \trowd\trgaph70\cellx3333\cellx6667\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 Dispatch\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Some related manuals seal hot bread immediately and assume a 23-minute delivery.\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Cool in a protected ventilated area; validate packing readiness. H2 uses explicit cooling, packing, vehicle loading, travel, handover and return assumptions.\cell \row \trowd\trgaph70\cellx3333\cellx6667\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 Retail bake\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 S026 offers a 15-minute par-bake option.\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 This edition schedules full baking at A. A qualified second bake, cooling/storage process and suitable B oven have not been established.\cell \row \pard\fs22\par \pard\sb200\sa140\keepn\b\fs28 BAG-H2-01 Direct-dough commercial baguette\b0\fs22\par \pard\sa120 Status: harmonized source adaptation, version H2, production trials required. Sources: S038 pp1\u8211?2, S030 pp1\u8211?2 and S027 pp1\u8211?2. Intended result: a lean, crisp-crusted, roughly 48\u8211?50 cm commercial baguette, with an evenly expanded crumb and consistent raw portion. It is not a claim to a protected French designation or to a guaranteed finished retail weight.\par \pard\sa120 Retain the source's nominal flour 100%, water 66%, salt 2% and instant yeast 0.5%. Scale to the required portions and allow 1% handling loss. Round flour upward to a whole gram, water to a gram, and salt/yeast to 0.1 g; recheck the resulting total. This avoids promising an additional whole piece from a rounded-down batch. The 40-piece pilot needs a suitably sized mixer; it is not automatically a permissible minimum load for the large spiral.\par \trowd\trgaph70\trhdr\cellx2500\cellx5000\cellx7500\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 \b Ingredient / specification\b0 \cell \pard\intbl\fs18 \b Baker %\b0 \cell \pard\intbl\fs18 \b Pilot 40 pieces, g\b0 \cell \pard\intbl\fs18 \b One load 80 pieces, g\b0 \cell \row \trowd\trgaph70\cellx2500\cellx5000\cellx7500\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 Le Choix du Boulanger flour; absorption/protein to verify\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 100\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 7,194\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 14,388\cell \row \trowd\trgaph70\cellx2500\cellx5000\cellx7500\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 Potable chilled water; ice included within this total\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 66\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 4,748\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 9,496\cell \row \trowd\trgaph70\cellx2500\cellx5000\cellx7500\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 Fine food-grade salt\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 2\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 143.9\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 287.8\cell \row \trowd\trgaph70\cellx2500\cellx5000\cellx7500\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 Nevada instant dry yeast\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 0.5\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 36.0\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 71.9\cell \row \trowd\trgaph70\cellx2500\cellx5000\cellx7500\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 Total weighed input\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 168.5 nominal\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 12,121.9\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 24,243.7\cell \row \pard\fs22\par \trowd\trgaph70\trhdr\cellx3333\cellx6667\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 \b Mass/yield measure\b0 \cell \pard\intbl\fs18 \b 40-piece pilot\b0 \cell \pard\intbl\fs18 \b 80-piece load\b0 \cell \row \trowd\trgaph70\cellx3333\cellx6667\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 Input g\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 12,121.90\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 24,243.70\cell \row \trowd\trgaph70\cellx3333\cellx6667\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 After 1% handling loss, g\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 12,000.68\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 24,001.26\cell \row \trowd\trgaph70\cellx3333\cellx6667\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 Raw pieces \u215? 300 g\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 40 \u215? 300 = 12,000\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 80 \u215? 300 = 24,000\cell \row \trowd\trgaph70\cellx3333\cellx6667\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 Unallocated dough after handling, g\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 0.68\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 1.26\cell \row \trowd\trgaph70\cellx3333\cellx6667\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 Bake loss illustration\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 15%; 255 g cooled per piece\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 15%; 255 g cooled per piece\cell \row \trowd\trgaph70\cellx3333\cellx6667\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 Before-reject cooled mass, kg\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 10.200\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 20.400\cell \row \trowd\trgaph70\cellx3333\cellx6667\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 Reject allowance: ceil(pieces \u215? 2%)\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 1 piece; 39 retained\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 2 pieces; 78 retained\cell \row \trowd\trgaph70\cellx3333\cellx6667\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 Retained saleable mass illustration, kg\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 9.945\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 19.890\cell \row \pard\fs22\par \pard\sa120 \u8220?Retained saleable\u8221? is a planning allowance, not a measured result or an order forecast. Rounding rejects upward makes the effective allowance 2.5% in these examples. Unsold stock is a separate commercial loss and is not silently included in this allowance. Record leftovers and their disposition; no extra loaf or unpriced rework is assumed.\par \pard\sa120 At 13\u8211?17% bake loss a 300 g portion finishes around 261\u8211?249 g. Therefore this plan does not establish a guaranteed 250 g net weight. Measure cooled weights and their variation before choosing a declared weight. If a particular minimum is required, design the portion allowance from actual worst-case process data and applicable requirements.\par \pard\sb200\sa140\keepn\b\fs24 Numbered process and observable endpoints\b0\fs22\par \pard\sa120 1. Before mixing, verify ingredient lots, clean scales, water supply, tray/rack fit, guards and steam controls. Record room, flour and water temperatures. Do not taste raw flour or dough. Prepare batch labels and weigh all ingredients separately; no improver, Milk tantalizer, milk, margarine or sugar belongs in BAG-H2-01.\par \pard\sa120 2. Start with most of the listed water, flour and yeast, mix gently for about 3 minutes, rest the hydrated dough for 10 minutes, then add salt and the balance of the listed water and mix about 5 minutes to moderate development. The 18-minute slot is a trial. Target source-derived final dough temperature 23\u8211?24\u176?C; adjust water temperature from measured friction and ambient conditions. Do not automatically use 4\u176?C water or a fixed ice percentage in every season. All ice must be food-grade, melt by the end of mixing and replace an equal mass of listed water.\par \pard\sa120 3. Transfer into a covered food-grade bulk bin. Allow a provisional 45-minute bulk fermentation. Require visible fermentation and extensibility, not a timer alone. At 0.5% instant yeast and this dough temperature, actual required time may be longer. Record the result; if the baseline under-ferments, extend bulk/proof and rerun the resource model rather than increasing yeast ad hoc.\par \pard\sa120 4. Divide and preshape in a 15-minute planning slot, checking pieces against 300 g. Keep pieces in numbered first-in/first-out order. The next 15-minute slot moulds those same pieces in the same order: at an even rate each piece has approximately 15 minutes between preshape and moulding. That rest overlaps division of later pieces; do not insert another full-batch 15 minutes unless the schedule is revised. Irregular work rates require timed subgroups and a new slot allowance.\par \pard\sa120 5. Mould gently, using verified roller settings and minimal measured dusting flour. Trial 48\u8211?50 cm lengths. Place seam-down, five per 60 \u215? 40 cm tray only if the finished width and airflow test pass. Dusting flour is an additional process quantity to weigh and cost; the dough formula does not include an unlimited dusting allowance.\par \pard\sa120 6. Load a verified proofer bay. Plan 60 minutes from the last tray loaded, near 26\u176?C and 75\u8211?80% relative humidity if the installed controls can maintain it. The first formed pieces begin expanding earlier. Check tray-to-tray consistency; a slowly recovering light indentation and expanded, aerated dough are guides. Bake at the appropriate endpoint. The schedule includes a further 10-minute scoring/loading slot; dough must tolerate that actual elapsed time. Record proof exit and oven entry separately.\par \pard\sa120 7. Preheat using the oven manual and a measured lead time. A trial starting point inherited from the source is 240\u176?C preheat, about 220\u176?C baking and 22 minutes for this size. Commission a steam programme through the working injection system; the source's 15\u8211?20-second pulse is not a universal setting. Score before loading, following the shaping style and a blade-handling procedure. Never throw water into the diesel oven or improvise the steam plumbing. Use the manufacturer's damper procedure to finish the crust.\par \pard\sa120 8. Check even colour, expansion and fully set crumb using cooled cut samples as well as the established bake controls. Unload with appropriate heat protection. Log recovery to the next qualified loading condition, rather than assuming the thermostat display proves recovery. Reserve 3 minutes to unload and 5 minutes to recover in the model; replace these with measurements.\par \pard\sa120 9. Cool protected on racks. The 45-minute allowance is a trial, not automatic packing release. Check that packaging causes no condensation and the crust specification is acceptable. Pack in clean food-grade paper or the qualified pack; use protected ventilated transport crates. Do not tightly seal steaming bread, reuse raw-food containers or place bread directly against vehicle surfaces.\par \pard\sa120 10. Release by lot and measured count, then dispatch to B. Check transport hygiene, quantities, time and condition at handover. Plan same-production-day quality review under C05; no multi-day shelf life is established. Retail replenishment follows actual sales and available display space. Segregate underbaked, damaged or otherwise rejected pieces; record any food-safe alternative use as a separate authorised product, not hidden yield.\par \pard\sa120 Allergens: wheat/gluten; review flour processing aids, yeast and shared-equipment labels for additional allergens or cross-contact. No allergen-free claim is made. C01 and C05 remain applicable; filled baguettes additionally require the relevant meat, egg, dairy and sauce controls.\par \pard\sb200\sa140\keepn\b\fs24 Cost audit and labour distinction\b0\fs22\par \trowd\trgaph70\trhdr\cellx2500\cellx5000\cellx7500\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 \b Input\b0 \cell \pard\intbl\fs18 \b One-load amount\b0 \cell \pard\intbl\fs18 \b Confirmed rate\b0 \cell \pard\intbl\fs18 \b Known FCFA\b0 \cell \row \trowd\trgaph70\cellx2500\cellx5000\cellx7500\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 Flour\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 14.388 kg\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 420/kg\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 6,042.96\cell \row \trowd\trgaph70\cellx2500\cellx5000\cellx7500\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 Salt\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 0.2878 kg\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 194.44/kg\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 55.96\cell \row \trowd\trgaph70\cellx2500\cellx5000\cellx7500\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 Nevada yeast\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 0.0719 kg\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 1,666.67/kg\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 119.83\cell \row \trowd\trgaph70\cellx2500\cellx5000\cellx7500\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 Water\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 9.496 kg\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 UNPRICED\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 UNPRICED\cell \row \trowd\trgaph70\cellx2500\cellx5000\cellx7500\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 Known ingredient subtotal\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 80 raw / 78 retained units\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Incomplete\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 6,218.75\cell \row \pard\fs22\par \pard\sa120 The known subtotal is 79.73 FCFA per planned retained unit. It excludes water, dusting flour, consumables, packaging, energy, paid labour, transport and unsold stock. No complete margin or selling-price recommendation follows from it. A 10% increase in currently priced inputs adds 7.97 FCFA per retained unit; 10% fewer sold units increases the same batch-cost allocation by 11.11% before whole-unit rounding.\par \pard\sa120 Reserve 35 staff-minutes per batch for M1 preweighing, mixer supervision, transfer and cleaning; 20 for D2 division/bench cleaning; 20 for F3 moulding/loading/bench cleaning; 13 active minutes for O4 score/load and unload; and 25 for P5 packing and tray-set cleanup. This gives about 113 allocated staff-minutes per batch before opening/closing, quality monitoring, relief, walking, transport or paid waiting. It includes the supervised dough-rest interval and is not a measured stopwatch labour standard. Record hands-on labour separately. Cost actual paid staffed hours, including coverage and waiting; do not multiply 113 minutes by a wage and call it full campaign labour cost.\par \pard\sa120 The model's first-batch elapsed time from mixing start to packing release is 248 minutes, plus opening checks before mixing. Active labour and elapsed process time are different quantities. The staffing allocation is intentionally generous for a commissioning bakery and can be redesigned only after timed trials.\par \pard\sb200\sa140\keepn\b\fs28 Tray layout, rack count and capacity gates\b0\fs22\par \pard\sa120 Trial layout: orient baguette length along the 60 cm tray edge. Five pieces at up to 6 cm finished width occupy five parallel lanes across the 40 cm edge: centres at about 5, 12.5, 20, 27.5 and 35 cm. A 50 cm finished length leaves 5 cm at each end; 6 cm width leaves 2 cm outer margins and 1.5 cm inter-piece gaps. These are geometric trial allowances, not proof of adequate airflow, pan-channel fit or final expansion. Check the actual usable surface inside rims. If loaves spread wider, use four per tray and replan quantities.\par \pard {\pict\pngblip\picw1684\pich1190\picwgoal10000\pichgoal7067 }\par \pard\sa120 The accompanying tray-layout diagram is schematic. The full 16-tray test must check all levels, colour, clearance, steam distribution and rack weight. The partial commissioning load uses 8 trays \u215? 5 pieces, spread according to the oven manual; do not claim half the baking time because the load is halved.\par \trowd\trgaph70\trhdr\cellx3333\cellx6667\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 \b Constraint\b0 \cell \pard\intbl\fs18 \b H2 baseline requirement\b0 \cell \pard\intbl\fs18 \b What changes the plan\b0 \cell \row \trowd\trgaph70\cellx3333\cellx6667\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 Mixer\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 80-piece batch 24.244 kg dough, 14.388 kg flour\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Verify minimum/maximum dough mass and duty cycle; the reported 50 kg flour description is not a confirmed bowl or dough rating\cell \row \trowd\trgaph70\cellx3333\cellx6667\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 Moulding / division\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Two separate work surfaces/operators; 80 pieces in each 15-minute stage\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Slower actual throughput increases stage slots; revise rest and proof age\cell \row \trowd\trgaph70\cellx3333\cellx6667\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 Proofers\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Two independently usable bays, each holding one full 16-tray rack\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 60 min proof + 5 min bay turnover at 45 min starts needs two bays. At 90 min proof, two bays require cadence at least 47.5 min: trial 50 min, then recheck all stages\cell \row \trowd\trgaph70\cellx3333\cellx6667\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 Oven\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 10 min score/load + 22 bake + 3 unload + 5 recovery = 40 min reservation\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 45 min starts leave 5 min nominal slack. A measured 23 min recovery makes reservation 58 min and requires a slower programme\cell \row \trowd\trgaph70\cellx3333\cellx6667\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 Rack/tray sets\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Four active sets in steady operation; a fifth full set provides contingency\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 A set is occupied from mould/loading through proof, bake, cool, pack and 10-min cleanup: 180 min. At 45-min starts, four sets are the calculated minimum; five sets = 80 trays, ownership unconfirmed\cell \row \trowd\trgaph70\cellx3333\cellx6667\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 Cooling/packing space\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Two full-load equivalent positions for cooling/packing overlap\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Keep a separate dispatch staging area sized to the delivery waves; do not borrow proofer space\cell \row \trowd\trgaph70\cellx3333\cellx6667\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 Vehicle\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 One vehicle, assumed 85-minute loaded-to-ready round trip\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 5 load + 30 outward + 15 handover + 30 return + 5 clean/check. Driver and vehicle cannot be sent on two overlapping trips\cell \row \trowd\trgaph70\cellx3333\cellx6667\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 Power and fuel\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Measured connected electrical loads, priority cold stores and oven diesel consumption\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 20 kW inverter, 30 kWh nominal storage and 25 kW generator are reported; usable energy, electrical phase, surges and diesel litres/hour remain open\cell \row \pard\fs22\par \pard\sa120 Rack sets are not the same as the oven's one-rack capacity. A rack occupied by cooling bread cannot simultaneously carry the next proofed load. The fifth contingency set is a planning provision, not a finding that the bakery owns five racks. No purchase has been made or assumed.\par \pard\sa120 At five pieces/tray the nominal oven-only rate is 80 \u215? 60 / 40 = 120 pieces/hour. The planned 45-minute production cadence is 106.67 pieces/hour once the pipeline is filled. Neither rate applies from 02:00: the first-batch lead time, opening work, cooling, dispatch and end-of-shift cleaning remain. With only four pieces/tray, each load becomes 64; five/ten loads become 320/640 raw pieces before rejects if all other stage times still pass.\par \pard\sa120 If 505 is an actual sales requirement rather than the historical raw-output claim, distinguish the two. Seven full 80-piece loads give 560 raw and 546 retained pieces under the stated reject model. A calculated alternative is six full loads plus a separately scaled 38-piece last load: 6 \u215? 78 + (38 \u8722? 1 reject) = 505 retained pieces from 518 raw. That mixed-load option needs its own last-batch weighing and partial-rack test; it is not a fourth released programme or a recommendation to manufacture unsold surplus.\par \pard\sb200\sa140\keepn\b\fs28 Chronological production scenarios\b0\fs22\par \pard\sa120 All scenarios begin opening checks at 02:00 and first mixing at 02:20. Times are planning outputs; they are not proof that dough will be ready on those clocks. The 800-piece case extends the campaign at the same cadence; it does not claim faster fermentation or an unproven faster oven.\par \trowd\trgaph70\trhdr\cellx2500\cellx5000\cellx7500\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 \b Programme\b0 \cell \pard\intbl\fs18 \b Loads and cadence\b0 \cell \pard\intbl\fs18 \b Raw / retained pieces\b0 \cell \pard\intbl\fs18 \b Final pack release\b0 \cell \row \trowd\trgaph70\cellx2500\cellx5000\cellx7500\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 PLAN-BAG-P\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 2 \u215? 40; 90 min\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 80 / 78\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 07:58\cell \row \trowd\trgaph70\cellx2500\cellx5000\cellx7500\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 PLAN-BAG-N\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 5 \u215? 80; 45 min\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 400 / 390\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 09:28\cell \row \trowd\trgaph70\cellx2500\cellx5000\cellx7500\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 PLAN-BAG-H\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 10 \u215? 80; 45 min\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 800 / 780\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 13:13\cell \row \pard\fs22\par \pard\sb200\sa140\keepn\b\fs24 PLAN-BAG-P Commissioning programme\b0\fs22\par \trowd\trgaph70\trhdr\cellx1667\cellx3333\cellx5000\cellx6667\cellx8333\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 \b Batch\b0 \cell \pard\intbl\fs18 \b Mix\b0 \cell \pard\intbl\fs18 \b Bulk\b0 \cell \pard\intbl\fs18 \b Divide \u8594? mould\b0 \cell \pard\intbl\fs18 \b Proof bay / proof\b0 \cell \pard\intbl\fs18 \b Score/load \u8594? bake out\b0 \cell \row \trowd\trgaph70\cellx1667\cellx3333\c