10000\pard\intbl\fs18 \b Batch\b0 \cell \pard\intbl\fs18 \b Unload / recover done\b0 \cell \pard\intbl\fs18 \b Cooling\b0 \cell \pard\intbl\fs18 \b Packing / lot release\b0 \cell \pard\intbl\fs18 \b Rack free after clean\b0 \cell \row \trowd\trgaph70\cellx2000\cellx4000\cellx6000\cellx8000\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 1\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 05:28 / 05:33\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 05:28\u8211?06:13\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 06:13\u8211?06:28\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 06:38\cell \row \trowd\trgaph70\cellx2000\cellx4000\cellx6000\cellx8000\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 2\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 06:13 / 06:18\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 06:13\u8211?06:58\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 06:58\u8211?07:13\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 07:23\cell \row \trowd\trgaph70\cellx2000\cellx4000\cellx6000\cellx8000\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 3\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 06:58 / 07:03\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 06:58\u8211?07:43\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 07:43\u8211?07:58\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 08:08\cell \row \trowd\trgaph70\cellx2000\cellx4000\cellx6000\cellx8000\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 4\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 07:43 / 07:48\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 07:43\u8211?08:28\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 08:28\u8211?08:43\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 08:53\cell \row \trowd\trgaph70\cellx2000\cellx4000\cellx6000\cellx8000\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 5\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 08:28 / 08:33\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 08:28\u8211?09:13\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 09:13\u8211?09:28\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 09:38\cell \row \trowd\trgaph70\cellx2000\cellx4000\cellx6000\cellx8000\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 6\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 09:13 / 09:18\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 09:13\u8211?09:58\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 09:58\u8211?10:13\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 10:23\cell \row \trowd\trgaph70\cellx2000\cellx4000\cellx6000\cellx8000\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 7\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 09:58 / 10:03\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 09:58\u8211?10:43\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 10:43\u8211?10:58\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 11:08\cell \row \trowd\trgaph70\cellx2000\cellx4000\cellx6000\cellx8000\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 8\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 10:43 / 10:48\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 10:43\u8211?11:28\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 11:28\u8211?11:43\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 11:53\cell \row \trowd\trgaph70\cellx2000\cellx4000\cellx6000\cellx8000\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 9\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 11:28 / 11:33\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 11:28\u8211?12:13\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 12:13\u8211?12:28\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 12:38\cell \row \trowd\trgaph70\cellx2000\cellx4000\cellx6000\cellx8000\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 10\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 12:13 / 12:18\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 12:13\u8211?12:58\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 12:58\u8211?13:13\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 13:23\cell \row \pard\fs22\par \trowd\trgaph70\trhdr\cellx2000\cellx4000\cellx6000\cellx8000\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 \b Delivery wave\b0 \cell \pard\intbl\fs18 \b Batches / retained units\b0 \cell \pard\intbl\fs18 \b Load \u8594? depart\b0 \cell \pard\intbl\fs18 \b Arrival at B\b0 \cell \pard\intbl\fs18 \b Vehicle ready back at A\b0 \cell \row \trowd\trgaph70\cellx2000\cellx4000\cellx6000\cellx8000\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 1\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 1 / 78\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 06:28 \u8594? 06:33\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 07:03\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 07:53\cell \row \trowd\trgaph70\cellx2000\cellx4000\cellx6000\cellx8000\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 2\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 2,3 / 156\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 07:58 \u8594? 08:03\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 08:33\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 09:23\cell \row \trowd\trgaph70\cellx2000\cellx4000\cellx6000\cellx8000\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 3\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 4,5 / 156\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 09:28 \u8594? 09:33\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 10:03\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 10:53\cell \row \trowd\trgaph70\cellx2000\cellx4000\cellx6000\cellx8000\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 4\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 6,7 / 156\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 10:58 \u8594? 11:03\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 11:33\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 12:23\cell \row \trowd\trgaph70\cellx2000\cellx4000\cellx6000\cellx8000\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 5\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 8,9 / 156\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 12:28 \u8594? 12:33\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 13:03\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 13:53\cell \row \trowd\trgaph70\cellx2000\cellx4000\cellx6000\cellx8000\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 6\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 10 / 78\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 13:53 \u8594? 13:58\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 14:28\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 15:18\cell \row \pard\fs22\par \pard\sa120 Calculated simultaneous requirements for this finite campaign: 2 proofer bays; 4 active rack/tray sets; 2 full-load equivalent cooling/packing positions. Maximum packed staging wait before vehicle loading is 45 minutes. These waits affect crust quality and sales freshness and must be tested.\par \pard\sa120 The final delivery is later than the final bake because one vehicle must finish its earlier trip before collecting the last load. The workbook exposes that queue. Use preorders and measured afternoon demand; a larger campaign is not automatically a better commercial choice. If the market needs all 800 pieces early in the morning, this programme does not meet that requirement. A separately validated earlier start, fermentation-retardation process, capacity expansion or revised product mix would be needed. Provide shift relief and handovers; do not assign a single person to an unbroken extended shift.\par \pard\sb200\sa140\keepn\b\fs24 Day-before preparation and staffing\b0\fs22\par \pard\sa120 Opening allocation: M1 checks scales, ingredient labels and the mixer from 02:00\u8211?02:10, then preweighs batch 1 from 02:10\u8211?02:20. D2/F3 prepare clean work surfaces, bins and trays. O4 checks the oven and steam system before starting an approved preheat programme. A provisional 45-minute preheat lead would mean 04:08 for the default first scoring/loading slot at 04:53; actual required lead time and readiness override this illustration. Count preheat and standby fuel/electricity in campaign costs. Complete opening sanitation before exposed-food handling.\par \pard\sa120 BAG-H2-01 is direct dough and does not require a poolish. Before the night shift, arrange water-temperature control, ingredients, clean racks/trays, labelled bulk bins, dispatch crates, fuel and customer orders. Do not leave mixed dough overnight under this recipe.\par \pard\sa120 M1-B12 is a different poolish baguette. Its 300 g flour, 300 g water and 0.3 g yeast preferment per 1 kg total flour are part of the total formula. Its 12\u8211?16-hour maturation must be started the previous day and assessed for readiness. Do not use BAG-H2-01's clock or add a second full flour/water charge. M1-B13 is a softer baguette; S-B01 is another daily baguette formula. Each requires its own dough, proof, bake and dispatch validation before being assigned a production programme.\par \trowd\trgaph70\trhdr\cellx3333\cellx6667\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 \b Role\b0 \cell \pard\intbl\fs18 \b Reserved work\b0 \cell \pard\intbl\fs18 \b Coverage / staffing condition\b0 \cell \row \trowd\trgaph70\cellx3333\cellx6667\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 M1 mixer lead\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 10 min preweigh before mix; 18-min mix/rest supervision; 7-min transfer and clean\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 35 minutes reserved per batch. On the extended plan relief R6 covers all of batch 4 weighing/mixing/cleanup so M1 can take an uninterrupted break; further breaks require recorded coverage.\cell \row \trowd\trgaph70\cellx3333\cellx6667\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 D2 divider/preshaper\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 15-min division plus 5-min bench clean\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Separate from F3. Keep FIFO labels and weight checks; batch count assumes this rate can be maintained.\cell \row \trowd\trgaph70\cellx3333\cellx6667\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 F3 moulder/rack loader\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 15-min mould/load plus 5-min work-area clean\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Track first/last tray formation age; use a separate surface so cleaning does not obstruct D2.\cell \row \trowd\trgaph70\cellx3333\cellx6667\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 O4 oven/proof lead\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Proof endpoint checks, 10-min score/load, supervised bake, 3-min unload and recovery monitoring\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Dedicated to hot operations; do not use this person as the delivery driver. Arrange qualified relief during the extended campaign.\cell \row \trowd\trgaph70\cellx3333\cellx6667\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 P5 cooling/packing\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Cooling checks, 15-min pack, 10-min rack/tray cleanup; opening/closing support\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Packing and dispatch staging must remain separate from raw-food handling.\cell \row \trowd\trgaph70\cellx3333\cellx6667\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 R6 relief\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Named trained relief for break coverage and handovers\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Extended campaign needs planned staffing beyond uninterrupted single-worker shifts. Never double-book the relief person across simultaneous roles.\cell \row \trowd\trgaph70\cellx3333\cellx6667\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 Driver / B receiver\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Vehicle waves as listed; independent receiving person at B\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Load handover is not full receiving-staff capacity planning. Confirm vehicle/crate capacity for the largest wave and retailer storage.\cell \row \pard\fs22\par \pard\sa120 Treat the roles as the resource model, not proof of the exact payroll required. Named people, opening/closing periods, lawful shift arrangements, breaks and paid hours must be assigned before release. Short gaps between tasks are not automatically sufficient rest breaks. The workbook schedules production stages and vehicle use; the supervisor must also schedule quality checks, breaks and other products. The extended programme remains on hold if that staffing plan is not supplied.\par \pard\sb200\sa140\keepn\b\fs28 Purchasing, complete costing and sensitivity\b0\fs22\par \trowd\trgaph70\trhdr\cellx1667\cellx3333\cellx5000\cellx6667\cellx8333\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 \b Programme\b0 \cell \pard\intbl\fs18 \b Flour kg\b0 \cell \pard\intbl\fs18 \b Water kg\b0 \cell \pard\intbl\fs18 \b Salt kg\b0 \cell \pard\intbl\fs18 \b Yeast kg\b0 \cell \pard\intbl\fs18 \b Known subtotal FCFA\b0 \cell \row \trowd\trgaph70\cellx1667\cellx3333\cellx5000\cellx6667\cellx8333\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 PLAN-BAG-P\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 14.388\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 9.496\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 0.2878\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 0.0720\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 6,218.92\cell \row \trowd\trgaph70\cellx1667\cellx3333\cellx5000\cellx6667\cellx8333\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 PLAN-BAG-N\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 71.940\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 47.480\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 1.4390\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 0.3595\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 31,093.77\cell \row \trowd\trgaph70\cellx1667\cellx3333\cellx5000\cellx6667\cellx8333\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 PLAN-BAG-H\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 143.880\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 94.960\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 2.8780\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 0.7190\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 62,187.54\cell \row \pard\fs22\par \pard\sa120 These are campaign consumption quantities, not instructions to buy a full bag/carton for every batch. Flour bags are 50 kg; yeast packs are 450 g. Deduct usable opening stock, choose a documented stock buffer, then round purchasing to supplier packs. Record chilled-water/ice energy, dusting flour and leftovers separately. Never add ice on top of the recipe water allowance.\par \pard\sa120 The editable workbook leaves water, packaging, dusting/consumables, electrical energy, diesel, variable staffing and transport blank until supplied. A genuinely zero cost must be explicitly entered as zero. Full variable campaign cost and contribution stay unavailable while required fields are blank. All paid staffing relevant to the campaign must be included once; do not add both a full shift and the same batch labour again.\par \pard\sa120 No selling price is imposed. Enter a candidate price and expected sold units only after a customer and outlet check. Contribution is revenue less complete variable cost; fixed rent, depreciation, financing and other fixed expenses still separate it from net profit. Cold storage and other products may share power and labour; document an allocation instead of assuming baguettes use the entire generator or that all energy is free solar power at 02:00.\par \pard\sa120 Sensitivity checks to run before release: 10% flour-price increase; lower actual sold units; 4 instead of 5 pieces/tray; proof 90 instead of 60 minutes; slower moulding; recovery 23 instead of 5 minutes; longer cooling; and delayed vehicle return. A resource conflict means the schedule is invalid until recalculated, not permission to hold proofed dough indefinitely.\par \pard\sb200\sa140\keepn\b\fs28 Contingencies, quality and release records\b0\fs22\par \trowd\trgaph70\trhdr\cellx5000\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 \b Trigger\b0 \cell \pard\intbl\fs18 \b Action\b0 \cell \row \trowd\trgaph70\cellx5000\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 Proof not ready\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Bake by dough endpoint; record the extension, hold the next mix if needed and recalculate bay/cadence requirements. Do not compress bulk or proof to catch up.\cell \row \trowd\trgaph70\cellx5000\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 Dough ready before oven\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Stop further starts; assess the batch with the lead baker. No unverified fridge/retarder shortcut or repeated arbitrary knock-back is prescribed.\cell \row \trowd\trgaph70\cellx5000\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 Power or diesel interruption\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Stop machinery safely, protect cold stores and record dough stage/time/temperature. Follow equipment restart procedures. Decide batch disposition from condition; recalculate the queue before restarting.\cell \row \trowd\trgaph70\cellx5000\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 Slow recovery / pale or uneven bake\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Measure loaded oven recovery and map tray levels. Reduce load or revise oven cycle. Do not direct combustion exhaust toward food, staff or the street.\cell \row \trowd\trgaph70\cellx5000\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 Moulding tears / sticking\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Check relaxation, flour absorption, dough temperature, roller gaps and measured dusting. Do not add flour or oil without logging the formula change.\cell \row \trowd\trgaph70\cellx5000\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 Weight / reject variance\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Check scales and cooled samples across trays. Recalculate portions, handling loss, bake loss and rejects from measurements; do not sell an assumed net weight.\cell \row \trowd\trgaph70\cellx5000\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 Cooling or packaging condensation\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Delay packing until release criteria pass; expand protected cooling space or slow starts. Record the delay and its rack impact.\cell \row \trowd\trgaph70\cellx5000\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 Delivery delay / low sell-through\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Keep protected staging, notify the receiving team through normal business procedures, reduce subsequent production and update sold-unit costing. Do not make additional batches solely to keep the oven busy.\cell \row \pard\fs22\par \pard\sa120 For each trial record: recipe/version; date; batch; operator/relief; ingredient lots and weighed masses; room/flour/water/dough temperatures; actual mix end; bulk start/end; first/last divide and mould; proof start/end and actual temperature/humidity; score/load and bake times; steam programme; unloaded weight/count; recovery time; cooled sample weights; rejects/leftovers; packing release; tray/rack available time; staff hours; water/dusting/oil-free process consumables; electricity and diesel; dispatch/arrival/return; B receipt; sold/returned units; full cost; corrective action; reviewer.\par \pard\sa120 Run at least three independently acceptable trials of the selected load and cadence before treating the programme as an operating standard. The programme is conditional on demonstrated product quality, safe handling and resource availability. Reissue the schedule when recipe, portion, oven load, proof duration, staff or route changes.\par \pard\sb200\sa140\keepn\b\fs24 Technical reference and evidence limit\b0\fs22\par \pard\sa120 King Arthur's professional baguette material reinforces that fermentation, shaping and steam are process-specific. Its professional sourdough formula uses a different fermentation system and is not the recipe adopted here. The H2 numerical timings come from the audited local sources and explicit planning assumptions, not from a manufacturer validation of this oven. King Arthur professional baguette reference (https://www.kingarthurbaking.com/pro/formulas/sourdough-baguettes)\par \pard\sa120 The source register distinguishes the local documents from this external technical reference. C01\u8211?C05 and their authoritative references remain in the anthology. This new section establishes no new Cameroon legal limit, food shelf life or guaranteed output.\par \pard\sb200\sa140\keepn\b\fs28 H2 integration and verification record\b0\fs22\par \pard\sa120 H2 adds one traceable recipe, BAG-H2-01, and three planning scenarios to the 137 working cards and 792 H1 coverage records. It preserves all earlier formulas, variants, prices and unresolved source records. H1 remains unchanged. The corrected baguette section supersedes conflicting scheduling statements for BAG-H2-01 only; it does not rewrite another recipe's fermentation method.\par \pard\sa120 The programme has been checked for batch mass, integer portions, loss arithmetic, source discrepancies, nonoverlapping equipment bookings, two-bay proof allocation, rack/cooling peaks and serialized delivery trips. Passing those arithmetic checks does not validate the assumed cycle times, named staffing, product quality or customer demand. Open gates remain visible in the workbook and issue register.\par }